I have not seen this patch ? Where is it ?

> What happens with the ACPI speed tables with CPU upgrade BTW? 
> Are they hardcoded, or generated by the BIOS?

BIOS dynamically builds the _PSS object dependent on the 
processor(s) that it finds. If you upgrade to a processor
that is so new that the BIOS does not know about it, the 
BIOS will not build any _PSS objects as it does not know what
to put in them. In this case, it is time for a BIOS upgrade.

